Simulated **Unitree G1 (29-DoF) with Inspire RH56E2 hands** walking up to a desk from widely randomised start poses and
picking up a red cylinder placed anywhere across the middle 60 % of the desk with the right hand (walk → stop → grasp →
lift). Isaac Sim 5.1 / Isaac Lab, built on [unitree_sim_isaaclab](https://github.com/unitreerobotics/unitree_sim_isaaclab).

**This is scripted, simulator-only data, not human teleoperation.** Every episode was generated automatically by a
scripted expert that plans from simulator ground truth (object and robot pose). The ground truth was used only to
plan the motion; it is stored in the `eval.*` columns for evaluation and is not meant as a policy input.

**Why this version:** an ACT policy trained on our earlier dataset
[g1_inspire_walk_far_grasp_desk065_scripted_v2](https://huggingface.co/datasets/jammin0319/g1_inspire_walk_far_grasp_desk065_scripted_v2)
(cylinder only at y −0.30…−0.10 m, robot starts within ±0.3 m sideways) walked to the same stance whatever the cylinder
position: 1/10 successes when the cylinder was moved across the desk. This version randomises both much more widely.

- **Task:** "walk to the desk and pick up the red cylinder" (one task). Desk 1.5 m wide, top height **0.65 m**; cylinder
  diameter 6 cm, height 0.12 m.
- **Episodes:** {n_eps} successful episodes, {n_frames:,} frames ({len_min}–{len_max} per episode), 25 fps. Only successes
  are included (cylinder lifted ≥ 5 cm, robot not fallen).
- **Randomisation (world frame, desk centre at y = 0):** robot start x −1.0 to −0.4 m, **y −1.0 to +1.0 m**, yaw ±15°;
  cylinder x 0.98–1.08 m, **y −0.45 to +0.45 m** (20–80 % of the desk width). In this data: start y (pelvis at the first frame, after the robot settles from the reset) {sy_min:+.2f} to
  {sy_max:+.2f} m, cylinder y {oy_min:+.2f} to {oy_max:+.2f} m; the stand pose is {lat_min:.2f}–{lat_max:.2f} m sideways and
  {fwd_min:.2f}–{fwd_max:.2f} m ahead of the start.
- **Walking:** {n_walk1} of {n_eps} episodes are one continuous walk followed by standing and grasping; episodes
  that stopped off target and re-approached were removed by the stability filter. Median {walk_med} walking frames = {walk_med_s:.1f} s. For large sideways
  offsets the expert heads for a point 0.8 m in front of the stand pose with the body turned towards the walking direction
  (at most 40°), then faces the desk for the final approach; near the line it walks facing the desk with a sideways
  component.
- **Selection:** the first {n_eps} episodes that passed a stability filter (success, pelvis tilt ≤ 7°, pelvis height
  ≥ 0.745 m, roll/pitch rate ≤ 1.0 rad/s) out of {n_rec} recorded.
- **Locomotion:** the official Unitree whole-body locomotion policy, driven by velocity commands that are recorded in
  `action.loco_cmd` = [vx, vy, wz, height]: the command the locomotion policy actually consumed at that step
  (captured inside the simulator where the policy reads it), so a model can drive walking by predicting it
  (`meta/modality.json` → action `base_command` = vx, vy, wz). The policy ignores `height` (always 0.8).
  When executing: the official policy resets the command to zero after every read, so re-publish the predicted
  command to `rt/run_command/cmd` at ≥ 50 Hz until the next prediction; it does not step for |vx| ≲ 0.3 m/s.
- **Arm/hand actions:** `action` (26) = left arm 7, right arm 7, left hand 6, right hand 6 joint position targets,
  applied by the simulator in the step following the observation. `action.hand_binary` = [left_close, right_close].
  Joint order is in `meta/info.json`; `meta/modality.json` gives the GR00T-style grouping.
- **Cameras (640×480, AV1):** head stereo `cam_left_high` / `cam_right_high` and wrist cameras `cam_left_wrist` /
  `cam_right_wrist` (RealSense D405 model). Intrinsics, distortion and mounting are in `meta/info.json` → `camera_params`.
- **Other columns:** `observation.base_vel` (body-frame linear/angular velocity), `observation.sim_time`,
  `eval.object_pos_w`, `eval.contact_force_total`, `eval.fallen`.

**Limitations:** simulation only; the scripted motions are smoother and more repetitive than human demonstrations.
The expert still stops at nearly the same pose relative to the cylinder (tolerance 4 cm forward, 3 cm sideways), so
reaching from a clearly offset stance is not covered. The RH56E2 hand model is a simulation approximation.

Format: LeRobot dataset v2.1 (lerobot 0.3.3), checked with the LeRobot v2.1 loader and the Isaac-GR00T N1.7
`LeRobotEpisodeLoader`. Load with `LeRobotDataset("jammin0319/g1_inspire_walk_wide_grasp_desk065_scripted_v3")`.
